From: Custom V4L2 HW Encode - Codec Filter Flags
Subject: Add command-line flags to disable VP8 or H264 encoding

Adds flags to filter WebRTC encoder codecs by failing encoder creation
(rather than removing from capabilities, which breaks setCodecPreferences):

Complete disable (HW + SW) - fails encoder creation, forces fallback:
  --webrtc-disable-vp8      Disable VP8 entirely (forces H264)
  --webrtc-disable-h264     Disable H264 entirely (forces VP8)

HW-only disable (keeps SW fallback):
  --webrtc-disable-vp8-hw   Disable VP8 HW only
  --webrtc-disable-h264-hw  Disable H264 HW only

Useful for testing/debugging codec-specific issues.
Ported from Chromium 117 to 129.0.6668.100.

Apply AFTER chromium-v4l2-hw-encode-129.patch

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [i.MX specific]

